nger than a  hero but as the fight progresses and the  Hulk keeps getting angrier the Hulk's  increasing strength puts him over the  edge at the end we get the Hulk uttering  his famous catchphrase for the first  time on screen and dare we say it it's  smashing in the comics the Hulk's most  persistent bow isn't a super villain  it's the United States military led by  general Thaddeus Thunderbolt Ross The  Incredible Hulk gave us a great example  of this conflict when the army corners  Bruce Banner on a college campus forcing  him to Hulk out and smash his way  through them and smash he does while  this Hulk doesn't express quite as much  physical power as later versions the  battle does a good job showing us  exactly what he's capable of  he's merely annoyed by the bullets and  even Tony Stark's sonic weapons just  increases rage when he sees Betty in  distress we also get a kind of preview  of Captain America when pre abomination  Emil  skee makes a bad choice of trying to  take the whole called solo with his new  super soldier abilities and gets punted  into a tree for his troubles the Hulk's  epic domination of Loki at the end of  The Avengers is an absolute landmark in  the nfinity saga it is first and  foremost one of the funniest scenes in  the MCU the comedy is the main reason  the scene is so memorable  but it actually provides a perfect  climax to one of the film's themes  throughout the Avengers we're hearing  from less Super characters like Nick  Fury who are talking about how the world  is struggling to react to all of these  Thunder gods and unfrozen super soldiers  who are suddenly showing up the Hawks  abrupt and merciless thrashing if Loki  is the perfect reflection of what Nick  Fury is talking about not only have  these heroes become people who can't be  matched by ordinary humans not even an  arrogant alien calling himself a God can  compare to them a lot of people had a  lot of problems with 2015's Avengers age  of Ultron but the Hulk's battle w